### FHIR Parser & Canonical Mapping (`com.medisense.abdm.parser`)

#### [NEW] [FhirBundleParser.java](file:///e:/agent/src/main/java/com/medisense/abdm/parser/FhirBundleParser.java)
- Uses HAPI FHIR R4 to parse FHIR Bundles:
  - **Observation**: extracts test name (`code.text`/`display`), value (`valueQuantity.value`), unit (`valueQuantity.unit`), reference range (`low`/`high`), interpretation (`N`/`L`/`H` -> `NORMAL`/`BORDERLINE`/`ABNORMAL`).
  - **MedicationRequest**: extracts drug name (`medicationCodeableConcept.text`/`display`), dosage instruction (`dosageInstruction[0].text`), timing, duration (`dispenseRequest.expectedSupplyDuration`).
  - **DiagnosticReport**: extracts linked lab observations.

---

### Async Callback Controller (`com.medisense.abdm.controller`)

#### [NEW / MODIFY] [AbdmCallbackController.java](file:///e:/agent/src/main/java/com/medisense/abdm/AbdmCallbackController.java)
- REST controller with async processing:
  - `POST /abdm/callback/consent/notify`: processes consent grant/deny. Immediately returns HTTP 202 Accepted. If GRANTED -> triggers `HealthRecordFetchService`. If DENIED -> updates status and notifies user to use PDF upload.
  - `POST /abdm/callback/health-info`: processes encrypted health record callback. Decrypts payload, parses FHIR bundle via `FhirBundleParser`, persists extracted `LabReportValue` and `Prescription` records, and returns HTTP 202 Accepted.

